            <ArticleTitle>Consensus for the use of fibrates in the treatment of dyslipoproteinemia and coronary heart disease. Fibrate Consensus Group.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>912-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The hypolipidemic action of fibrates has recently been shown to involve the activation of peroxisome proliferator activated receptors establishing a molecular mechanism for this class of drugs. Increasing clinical trial evidence supports the efficacy of fibrates in the treatment of dyslipoproteinemias, particularly in patients with hypertriglyceridemia and low high-density lipoproteins.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
